\subsection*{10.1.4 Binomial Coefficients}

We now show how to compute \textit{binomial coefficients} as another example of how to eliminate recursion by specifying the order of evaluation. The binomial coefficients are the most important class of counting numbers, where $\binom{n}{k}$ counts the number of ways to choose $k$ things out of $n$ possibilities.

