Sending an additional unit of flow along directed edge $(i, j)$ reduces the residual capacity of edge $(i, j)$ but \textit{increases} the residual capacity of edge $(j, i)$. Thus, the act of augmenting a path requires modifying both forward and reverse edges for each link on the path.

\begin{verbatim}
void augment_path(flow_graph *g, int start, int end, int volume) {
    edgenode *e; /* edge in question */
    if (start == end) {
        return;
    }
    e = find_edge(g, parent[end], end);
    e->flow += volume;
    e->residual -= volume;
    e = find_edge(g, end, parent[end]);
    e->residual += volume;
    augment_path(g, start, parent[end], volume);
}
\end{verbatim}

