The \textit{union--find} data structure represents each subset as a ``backwards'' tree, with pointers from a node to its parent. Each node of this tree contains a set element, and the \textit{name} of the set is taken from the key at the root, as shown in Figure 8.5. For reasons that will become clear, we also keep track of the number of elements in the subtree rooted in each vertex $v$:

\begin{verbatim}
typedef struct {
