mov num2, eax
\end{verbatim}

Although the following example is clearly less efficient than the above, it helps demonstrate how the \textit{esi} and \textit{edi} registers can be used to transfer data between memory locations and will be helpful in subsequent examples of array processing:

\begin{verbatim}
