Clearly the first example is simpler, but the code above accomplishes the same task and can be expanded to transferring elements of an array. Given how the \texttt{esi} and \texttt{edi} registers work, can they be used to implement some of the array functions introduced previously? The answer is yes. As an example, consider the previous C segment which summed the elements of an array,
\begin{verbatim}
sum = 0;
for(i=0; i<3; i++)
