Consider Figure 2.9, showing a set of points (left) admitting a good linear fit, with correlation $r = 0.94$. The corresponding residuals $r_{i} = y_{i} - f(x_{i})$ are plotted on the right. The variance of the $y$ values on the left $V(y) = 0.056$, substantially greater than the variance $V(r) = 0.0065$ on the right. Indeed,

